WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:13.380
53. Unusual Taboos. All cultures have taboos, things that are not allowed. Many taboos come

2
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.540
from religion and ancient traditions. What may be perfectly normal in one culture can

3
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:26.980
be terribly offensive in another. Many taboos are about food and clothing. Are you eating

4
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:34.460
now? What time is it? In Portugal, you shouldn't eat oranges at night. In Cape Verde, they

5
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:40.580
say the same thing about sweet potatoes. Some taboos are about what you shouldn't eat. In

6
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:49.180
America, eating dog or horse meat is taboo, as is eating most insects. In other places,

7
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:55.220
these foods are fine. Many people in India would never eat beef, but in most of the rest

8
00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:02.860
of the world, people raise cows for meat. The way people eat is also ruled by taboos. In China,

9
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:09.060
you can eat with your mouth open, whereas in Europe, this is rude. In many parts of the world,

10
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:15.860
eating with the left hand is taboo because it is used for washing yourself. Clothing taboos

11
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:22.980
often show social status. Many cultures use colors to show rank. In ancient Rome,

12
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:31.060
only senators could wear purple. Some taboos are about what skin people can show. In the past,

13
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:39.940
to see a woman's ankle was taboo. Now we have bikinis. In India, traditional saris show women's

14
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:47.060
stomachs, but these clothes would be taboo in much of the Middle East. And in Tonga, it is illegal

15
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:53.700
for a man to go without a shirt in public. Understanding taboos helps us understand other

16
00:01:53.700 --> 00:02:00.300
cultures' histories since most taboos come from the distant past. Learning about other cultures'

17
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:08.460
taboos also helps us understand our own. After all, any one of our taboos could seem strange

18
00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.460
to a foreigner.
